PostgreSQL post-load sort strategy:
  BEGIN;
  CREATE TABLE {t}_ctas_sort AS SELECT * FROM {t} ORDER BY col;
  DROP TABLE {t};
  ALTER TABLE {t}_ctas_sort RENAME TO {t};
  COMMIT;
Verify: does this preserve indexes/constraints created by schema setup? Likely not -
the DROP removes the table and its constraints. The base class apply_ctas_sort runs
after data load but the schema (CREATE TABLE + indexes) was applied earlier in the
run. Determine whether constraints must be re-applied or if COPY-based loading makes
them unnecessary for benchmark purposes.
